You Will:

• support the Financial Controller in the financial supervision of selected foreign subsidiaries;

• maintain day-to-day contact with local finance staff and external accounting offices, escalating issues to the Financial Controller;

• support the preparation of financial data for consolidation, reporting and management purposes;

• prepare financial analyses, reports and forecasts under the guidance of the Financial Controller;

• gather reporting relevant data from specific sources and verify its completeness;

• support monitoring of accounts receivable and credit risk;

• support cash flow forecasting and payment management;

• support documentation of controlling processes and financial procedures within the Capital Group;

• effectively cooperate with the central finance team, business departments and profit center managers;

• strive to improve financial processes;

• support ad hoc tasks.

Desired Experience:&nbsp;

• bachelor's degree in Finance, Accounting, or similar area;

• working experience of 1 to 3 years in finance, controlling, accounting or audit;

• basic knowledge of accounting and corporate finance;

• good understanding of financial reporting principles;

• working knowledge of office applications especially Google Sheets/Excel;

• strong analytical and organizational skills;

• very good communication skills;

• personality: proactive, meticulous, attentive to detail, team player, eager to learn, open to feedback, able to work with deadlines under pressure;

• fluent in English.

Nice to have:

• working knowledge of IFRS;

• basic knowledge of tax law;

• experience working in a shared service organization or a multinational group structure.

We Offer:&nbsp;

• ability to cooperate in a truly international environment with HQ in Poland;

• opportunity to gain experience at the head office level of a multinational group rather than at a subsidiary;

• direct mentoring and support from experienced Financial Controllers, with a clear path to develop into a Financial Controller role;

• friendly and supporting atmosphere;

• stable, long-term cooperation based on a B2B contract or contract of mandate.

